<head><!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Privacy Policy – Animal World</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #fffdf6;
      --card: #ffffff;
      --sky: #d6f0ff;
      --sky-deep: #0284c7;
      --mint: #d1fae5;
      --mint-deep: #15803d;
      --sun: #fef3c7;
      --peach: #ffedd5;
      --ink: #1e293b;
      --muted: #475569;
      --border: #e2e8f0;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 24px 16px 48px;
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--sky) 0%, var(--bg) 280px, var(--bg) 100%);
      color: var(--ink);
      line-height: 1.65;
    }

    .container {
      max-width: 820px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .hero {
      background: var(--card);
      border: 2px solid var(--sky);
      border-radius: 24px;
      padding: 28px 28px 24px;
      box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.06);
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    .badge {
      display: inline-block;
      background: var(--mint);
      color: var(--mint-deep);
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      padding: 6px 14px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 8px;
      font-size: 2rem;
      line-height: 1.2;
      color: var(--ink);
    }

    .subtitle {
      margin: 0 0 18px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 1.02rem;
    }

    .meta-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr));
      gap: 12px;
      background: #f8fafc;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 14px 16px;
      font-size: 0.94rem;
    }

    .meta-item strong {
      display: block;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-bottom: 2px;
    }

    .meta-item span,
    .meta-item code {
      color: var(--ink);
      font-weight: 600;
      word-break: break-word;
    }

    code {
      background: var(--sun);
      padding: 2px 7px;
      border-radius: 6px;
      font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
      font-size: 0.9em;
    }

    .card {
      background: var(--card);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 20px;
      padding: 22px 26px;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.03);
    }

    h2 {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      color: var(--sky-deep);
    }

    p {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }

    p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    ul {
      margin: 8px 0 0;
      padding-left: 20px;
    }

    li {
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }

    li:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .highlight-box {
      background: var(--peach);
      border-left: 4px solid #ea580c;
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 14px 16px;
      margin-top: 12px;
      font-size: 0.96rem;
    }

    footer {
      text-align: center;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.88rem;
      margin-top: 26px;
    }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      .hero, .card {
        padding: 18px;
      }
      h1 {
        font-size: 1.65rem;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="container">
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="badge">100% Offline &amp; Kid-Safe • No Ads • No Data Collection</div>
      <h1>Privacy Policy for Animal World</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">
        This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Manoj</strong> handles information in the
        <strong>Animal World</strong> Android application designed for children aged 4–6 years.
      </p>

      <div class="meta-grid">
        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>App Name</strong>
          <span>Animal World</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Package Name</strong>
          <code>com.aistudio.animalworld.kxpqzm</code>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Developer</strong>
          <span>Manoj</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Effective Date</strong>
          <span>November 16, 2026</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>1. Overview &amp; Commitment to Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Animal World</strong> is an offline educational mobile application built specifically for
        young children (ages 4–6) to learn about animals, listen to animal sounds, hear voice
        pronunciations, read fun facts, and play interactive quizzes and mini-games.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are committed to protecting children's privacy in accordance with the Google Play Families
        Policy and applicable children's privacy laws (including COPPA and GDPR-K).
      </p>
      <div class="highlight-box">
        <strong>Summary:</strong> Animal World does <strong>NOT</strong> collect, store on external
        servers, sell, or share any personal information from children or parents.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>2. Information We Do Not Collect</h2>
      <p>Animal World works offline without user accounts or login. We do not collect or request:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Names, email addresses, phone numbers, dates of birth, or home addresses.</li>
        <li>Device identifiers, Advertising IDs, IP addresses, or analytics telemetry.</li>
        <li>Photos, videos, microphone recordings, contacts, or precise/coarse location data.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>3. Local On-Device Storage Only</h2>
      <p>
        To save your child's learning journey, Animal World stores non-personal progress and
        preference data strictly on your own device using Android's local DataStore storage:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Which animals have been explored, total stars earned, quizzes completed, and best quiz score.</li>
        <li>Parent audio preferences (Sound Effects, Background Music, and Voice Pronunciation toggles).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This data never leaves your device. Parents can erase all saved progress at any time via
        <strong>Parent Settings → Reset Learning Progress</strong> (protected by a math Parental Gate)
        or by uninstalling the app.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>4. Permissions &amp; Offline Audio</h2>
      <p>
        Animal World requests <strong>zero dangerous or sensitive Android permissions</strong> (such as
        Camera, Location, Microphone, Contacts, or External Storage).
      </p>
      <p>
        Animal sound effects and gentle background music are synthesized locally on-device, and animal
        names/facts are spoken using Android's built-in on-device Text-to-Speech (TTS) engine.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>5. No Ads, Analytics, or External Links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No Advertisements:</strong> Animal World contains zero third-party ad networks or banner/video ads.</li>
        <li><strong>No In-App Purchases:</strong> All animals, quizzes, and mini-games are included offline without paid prompts.</li>
        <li><strong>No Third-Party Tracking:</strong> No third-party analytics, crash-reporting trackers, or social media SDKs are used.</li>
        <li><strong>No Child-Accessible External Links:</strong> There are no outbound web links inside the child-facing experience.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>6. Parental Controls</h2>
      <p>
        The <strong>Parent Settings</strong> area is separated behind a math-based Parental Gate so young
        children cannot accidentally modify audio settings or reset their learning progress.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>7. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we ever update Animal World in a way that changes how information is handled, we will update
        this Privacy Policy and revise the "Effective Date" at the top of this page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>8. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you are a parent, guardian, or reviewer with any questions about this Privacy Policy or
        <strong>Animal World</strong> (<code>com.aistudio.animalworld.kxpqzm</code>), please contact the developer:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Developer Name:</strong> Manoj</li>
        <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:manodrx90@gmail.com">manodrx90@gmail.com</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <footer>
      &copy; 2026 Manoj &bull; Animal World (<code>com.aistudio.animalworld.kxpqzm</code>)
    </footer>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
